You are analyzing hierarchical software requirements for cross level traceability.
Determine whether a traceability link exists between a High-Level Requirement (HLR) and a Low-Level Requirement (LLR).
A link exists if the LLR implements, refines, or decomposes the HLR.
High-Level Requirement:
  Summary: Enforce SecureSigningAlgorithmForSignedJwtEnforceExecutor to private-key-jwt clients regardless their option
  Description: This ticket is the follow-up ticket for .
`SecureSigningAlgorithmForSignedJwtEnforceExecutor` should be enforced to the client whose authentication method is private-key-jwt regardless of this executor's option `isRequireClientAssertion`'s value.
Low-Level Requirement:
  Summary: SecureSigningAlgorithmForSignedJwtEnforceExecutor polishing for FAPI
  Description: Regarding `SecureSigningAlgorithmForSignedJwtEnforceExecutor`, it contains these potential issues, which I think will be good to address for the FAPI:
- It will fail if "client_assertion" parameter is not provided. However FAPI allows also client authentication with x509 client authenticator, which does not use "client_assertion" parameter. Hence all clients using x509 will currently fail this executor even if client is FAPI compliant. I wonder that we can possibly add option "Require Client Assertion". If false, the executor will just allow request to continue in case that "client_assertion" parameter is not present . I think that this does not contradicts FAPI as it means that request is authenticated with x509 client authenticator then (they are supposed to be other executors to check client authentication method)
- Just for the sake of simplicity (and maybe slightly better security protection), it will be probably good to remove this check from method `SecureSigningAlgorithmForSignedJwtEnforceExecutor.VerifySecureSigningAlgorithm` 
{code}
 if (signatureAlgorithm == null) {
  logger.trace("Signing algorithm not specified explicitly.");
  return;
 }
{code}
The reason is that "alg" claim must be present in JWS according to the specification . For the case it is not present, I guess there may be even earlier the NullPointerException on this line
{code}
String alg = jws.getHeader().getAlgorithm().name();
{code}
